 "notes": "The hospital antibiogram summarised in the UCMS and GTB Hospital antimicrobial policy 2026-27, January to December 2025, as ranked percent-susceptible lists for each infection type. The policy prints no isolate numbers, so every figure here is shown in grey, is never pooled and is not used by syndrome reasoning; the lists also include organisms that were probably isolated only a few times. Infection types are filed under the specimen they are cultured from: bloodstream infections as blood, urinary as urine, respiratory as respiratory, skin and soft tissue as pus, bone and joint as deep infections, and central nervous system as CSF; settings are not split (all settings). Several lists print figures out of their ranked order or pairs that cannot both be right (for example respiratory K. pneumoniae imipenem 79.2% with meropenem 0%); they are recorded as printed and the data checks mark them.",
